# NACA 64(1)-012 basic thickness form (half-thickness yt/c)   <-- DEFAULT thickness table
# Source: Abbott & von Doenhoff, "Theory of Wing Sections" (Dover, 1959), Appendix I,
#   "NACA 64(1)-012" (the same ordinates appear in NACA Report 824). 3 decimals in percent chord.
# Digital copy used: UIUC Airfoil Coordinates Database, file n64012.dat,
#   "NASA/LANGLEY 64-012 AIRFOIL", https://m-selig.ae.illinois.edu/ads/coord/n64012.dat
#   (downloaded 2026-10-22; raw file kept in data/downloads/n64012.dat).
# Leading-edge radius: not in the UIUC file, so it is not set here. The code then estimates
#   it from the first few table points (see README). A value can be added as "# le_radius = ...".
# columns: x/c  yt/c
